ut input, so I'd need to start the game first, then trace while the card is shown and the level loads. The level load happens after the card (~2s). So: play_input Start,Start (reach 1-1), then immediately trace 400 frames — but we might already be past the load.\n\nAlternatively: play_input Start (title->game card), then trace 600 frames; the load happens during the trace. Hmm, but Start needs the game unpaused.\n\nActually here's the reliable method: reset_emulator puts us on title. Then play_input: Start (12), wait 60, Start (12) — this begins the game and the card; the level loads right after. Then trace immediately catches the load. But the level load might be within the first ~60 frames after the card.\n\nHmm, let me think about the exact timing: After the second Start, the \"WORLD 1-1\" card shows for ~2s, then the level loads. If I trace right after the second Start, the load will occur within ~150 frames. So play_input Start,Start then trace 300 frames — should catch it.\n\nBut wait: the card display is part of the level-init state machine which INCLUDES the data load? The object data load at $9C22 happens at $902F (JSR $9C22) in the routine $9071 which is $0772=2? Actually $9071 is the entry for $0772=2, called after level init. Hmm.\n\nThe object data is loaded when the level actually starts (after the card), not during the card. So tracing after the card should catch $9C22 reading the pointer tables, but does it read the object data? $9C22 only reads the header (2 bytes). The object parser reads the object data as the camera scrolls.\n\nHmm, so the object data at $A690 is read only as the camera advances. And the parser reads ahead. So to catch reads, the camera must move. But trace has no input...\n\nUnless: during level start, the game pre-parses the first few pages. Let me trace $A690 during a fresh level start and see.\n\nAlternatively use trace_writes in read mode on the *whole* object region while the game naturally does something. Hmm.\n\nActually,