{"type":"text","text":"Done. Here's what I found and proved for **World 1-1**.\n\n## World 1-1 data locations (prgRom offsets, no header)\n\n| Part | prgRom offset | CPU | Length | End marker |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **Layout records** (ground/blocks/pipes) | `0x2690` | `$A690` | 98 bytes = 49 two-byte records | `$FD` at `0x26F2` |\n| **Enemy placements** | `0x1F01` | `$9F01` | 30 bytes | `$FF` at `0x1F1E` |\n\nThe two-byte area header sits at `0x268E` (`50 21`); the next area's data starts at `0x26F3` (layout) and `0x1F1F` (enemies).\n\n## How they're reached\n- At level start, `$9C22` reads the area header via `($E7),Y` and builds two 16-bit pointers from base/low/high table pairs:\n  - `$E7/$E8` (**layout**) from `$9D28`/`$9D2C`/`$9D4E` → `$A68E` (header) / `$A690` (records)\n  - `$E9/$EA` (**enemies**) from `$9CE0`/`$9CE4`/`$9D06` → `$9F01`\n- The layout is walked by the area parser at `$9508` using index `$072C` (`LDA ($E7),Y`, +2 per record, `$FD` checked at `$9516`).\n- Enemies are walked by the spawner at `$C147` using index `$0739` (`LDA ($E9),Y`, `$FF` checked at `$C14B`).\n\n## Proofs (each a one-byte ledgered prgRom write → reset → Start/Start → screenshot → `undo_edit`)\n- **Layout:** wrote `0x2696 = $FD` (record 3 byte0). Re-entering 1-1, the floating ? block at ~(176,88) was gone while every other object on screen was unchanged (baseline run has it). Restored `$99`.\n- **Enemies:** wrote `0x1F01 = $FF` (spawner's end-of-list byte). Re-entering and holding Right past the first Goomba's column to the first pipe, Mario survived and **no enemy appeared at all**. Restored `$1E`.\n\nRead traces backed both: `$A690` was read by PCs in `$95xx`/`$96xx`/`$9Bxx`, `$9F01` by PCs in `$C14x`–`$C1Bx`.\n\n## Bookkeeping\n- All ROM writes went into the throwaway hack `eval-sheet4-data`; both were `undo_edit`-ed, so its ledger is empty and the ROM bytes are back to original (`0x2696 = $99`, `0x1F01 = $1E` verified).\n- `record_mapping` level `1-1` (with both `rom_origins`) and note `1-1-area-data-tables` (pointer tables + loader/parser/spawner code) recorded, both `confidence: 1`, source `trace and ledgered write`.\n- `promote_mappings` called (2 discoveries promoted).\n- Switched back with `use_hack default`."}
